{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows","id":1219870,"title":"How problematic are Pure Tribes Vows?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-17T20:33:14-07:00","id":1219870,"title":"How problematic are Pure Tribes Vows?","content":"<b>I have a question how limiting are Oaths specific made by Pure Tribes, in real gameplay?</b> For example, I think about doing Predator Kings pack inside Forest Service. Can they use uniforms or personal weapons and <i>not</i> drop in Harmony each scene? Can they look human, most of the time, and not every time test their Harmony?<br /> <br /> <b>Side question:</b> I cannot find in 2E corebook how stated are Tribe Vows for Pure. Where are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T20:59:39-07:00","id":1219874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows#post1219870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I have a question how limiting are Oaths specific made by Pure Tribes, in real gameplay?</b> For example, I think about doing Predator Kings pack inside Forest Service. Can they use uniforms or personal weapons and <i>not</i> drop in Harmony each scene? Can they look human, most of the time, and not every time test their Harmony?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire-Touched have a pretty severe restriction, but it can be played around by a smart character. Predator Kings can get really screwed, since even getting them into a building is one way to break their ban apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Side question:</b> I cannot find in 2E corebook how stated are Tribe Vows for Pure. Where are they? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439788-pure-tribes-vows\">Previous thread you made answered this.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T21:58:41-07:00","id":1219878,"title":"","content":"I imagine second edition will change or at least adapt the bans, considering how the Pure have changed.<br /> <br /> Not honoring things of human craft can mean no walking in cities, but it can also just mean not paying undue respect to modern things. There's an entire lodge of Predator Kings devoted to living in cities and the example member is a high-functioning member of the upper class. That was first edition, with a stricter ban and different Harmony value, that included them and other Pure breaking the ban at Harmony 3-5 since they could ask for penance later.<br /> <br /> That said, a Predator King probably wouldn't bind themselves to a job in Forest Services, something they can do better an unhindered without anchoring themselves to a bureaucracy ultimately led by humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-18-2018, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T22:17:43-07:00","id":1219884,"title":"","content":"Tribal Bans have been...altered. It is a breaking point towards Flesh, yes. And it could come under the Ban condition, inflicting penalties to breaking it and earning beats whilst Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T22:20:00-07:00","id":1219885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219878#post1219878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine second edition will change or at least adapt the bans, considering how the Pure have changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e core has their bans in the antagonists section (though not in as fancy a manner as the forsaken tribes bans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T22:33:58-07:00","id":1219886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219885#post1219885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e core has their bans in the antagonists section (though not in as fancy a manner as the forsaken tribes bans).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah lets see. 'They have their tribal oaths just like we do, and it\u2019s a weakness worth exploiting. The Fire-Touched can never knowingly lie, so trick and mislead them with false information. The Ivory Claws cannot call an \u201cimpure\u201d Uratha their brother, so set rumors going that their allies come from Forsaken bloodlines and watch the rifts open up. The Predator Kings can\u2019t use the fruits of human labor, which puts them on the back foot already, but you can tighten the screws further \u2014 chase or lure them into human buildings, that sort of thing. Make them choose \u2014 break their oath or suffer.'<br /> <br /> They are a little different from first edition, though it's in-character so the perspective may not be spot on. It will be interesting to see how Shunned by the Moon expands on them. The 'fruits of human labor' thing is a pretty big weakness. Though like FallenEco pointed out, as its a break to the Flesh, with the Pure leaning towards the Spirit having tribal ban breaking bringing them up could probably help them maintain balance. They were sort of like the Circle of the Crone in first edition, willingly dropping their Harmony so they could pay penance for it later (instead of the Circle's dropping of Humanity to better understand it). I think they're supposed to have a different Harmony scale, though, or at least an Oath that has different Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-18-2018, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T22:58:40-07:00","id":1219889,"title":"","content":"Ask a Simple Question, wyrd... use the thread. Stop spamming us with new ones for your *simple questions*, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T00:58:40-07:00","id":1219896,"title":"","content":"Is it against community rules to suggest we should start reporting every topic started that better belongs in the simple questions thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T03:05:13-07:00","id":1219908,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219889#post1219889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask a Simple Question, wyrd... use the thread. Stop spamming us with new ones for your *simple questions*, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not 'simple topic', as literally <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> pointed above - and I will expand now.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219878#post1219878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not honoring things of human craft can mean no walking in cities, but it can also just mean not paying undue respect to modern things. There's an entire lodge of Predator Kings devoted to living in cities and the example member is a high-functioning member of the upper class. That was first edition, with a stricter ban and different Harmony value, that included them and other Pure breaking the ban at Harmony 3-5 since they could ask for penance later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> of living in building should be okay for Predator Kings - humans and werewolves were doing this before death of <i>Urfarah</i>. Probably usage of modern technology is outside of question. <b>So maybe Predator Kings can use lone, wooden hut in the woods? Or living in RV/camper vehicle?</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-18-2018, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T03:09:29-07:00","id":1219909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219884#post1219884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribal Bans have been...altered. It is a breaking point towards Flesh, yes. And it could come under the Ban condition, inflicting penalties to breaking it and earning beats whilst Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, so by Breaking Tribal Vows Pure are <i><b>gaining</b> <b>back</b></i> Harmony, and rising to Flesh? This is interesting - so typical Pure life is 'doing Totems slave service, going low on Harmony, and then break their own Bans so to regain to middle of Harmony' in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T03:13:59-07:00","id":1219910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219878#post1219878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, a Predator King probably wouldn't bind themselves to a job in Forest Services, something they can do better an unhindered without anchoring themselves to a bureaucracy ultimately led by humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more in line for the Predator Kings of 'We are forest rangers ( and so can kill you ), our Wolf-Blooded are running park from big office in center of it.' Using firearms is probably going under the Tribal Ban, but using uniform? It's only clothing - in <b>The Pure</b> book I saw Predator King splat image in clothing so should probably by okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T04:04:46-07:00","id":1219917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219908#post1219908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not 'simple topic', as literally <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> pointed above - and I will expand now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise that the simple question threads can handle both follow up questions and discussions (that I've repeatedly seen cover multiple pages while your threads rarely reach more than one)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T04:51:11-07:00","id":1219925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219908#post1219908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not 'simple topic', as literally <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> pointed above - and I will expand now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is a simple topic, wyrd. Like so many of your \u2018difficult\u2019 topics, it always boils down to you asking a question, receiving a couple of opinions, you then spam-posting your own thread as you turn each individual thought you have into separate posts. And 99% of the time the answer to your questions is \u2018whatever works best for your game.\u2019 And 100% of the time, the answer you choose to accept is \u2018whatever I felt like doing before I even asked the question.\u2019<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s play this game.<br /> <br /> Q - How limiting are Pure Oaths in gameplay?<br /> A - As limiting as every other tribal oath. If you break them, you\u2019ll have a breaking point. If you do it too often, you\u2019ll have a pissed off Firstborn patron.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s it. Everything else is just you talking yourself into fulfilling the concept you proposed you were going to do in the initial post.<br /> <br /> Now if you posted these questions in the \u2018Ask a Simple Question\u2019 thread, people would give you some quick answers. Job done. If you ask something that is legimately a more difficult question, rest-assured that people will be quick to offer that opinion and suggest that you spin it off into a bigger thread for discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T05:36:02-07:00","id":1219933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219925#post1219925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q - How limiting are Pure Oaths in gameplay?<br /> A - As limiting as every other tribal oath. If you break them, you\u2019ll have a breaking point. If you do it too often, you\u2019ll have a pissed off Firstborn patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what would be Breaking Points for Predator Kings Ban? Using Firearms/clothing/house?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T05:51:29-07:00","id":1219936,"title":"","content":"Anything made by humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T05:57:10-07:00","id":1219939,"title":"","content":"Depends on how the Storyteller chooses to interpret 'honor nothing' - in 1e I seem to recall it was elucidated upon as the intention being, as Bunyip says, use of anything made by humans, but I don't think the game will break or anything if an ST decides 'honoring' a thing means more than just using it, but considering it worthy in and of itself. One might decide that just entering a human dwelling to get shelter from the rain is fine, but that intentionally acquiring a human abode for long-term residence, being house-proud of it, etc, is more in breach of the ban.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut then, an ST's ability to interpret something is one of the great variables of any game, and will change from table to table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T06:47:18-07:00","id":1219947,"title":"","content":"Personally I would tend to go with the latter interpretation, going into a house to beat some Uratha hide should be something they might be unhappy with, but not something Predator Kings would flagellate themselves over, that\u2019s the Fire Touched\u2019s schtick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T06:57:35-07:00","id":1219950,"title":"","content":"Did humans make it, and is the Predator King using it to their advantage? Breaks Ban. Did the Uratha or anyone else make it, or the PK only interact with it as required for the hunt? Fine with Ban.<br /> <br /> Use a Gun? Breaks - probably, see below.<br /> Uniform? Unless the PK made it themselves, Breaks.<br /> Use a door? No break - extra safe if they <i>break</i> the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T07:04:16-07:00","id":1219955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219939#post1219939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how the Storyteller chooses to interpret 'honor nothing' - in 1e I seem to recall it was elucidated upon as the intention being, as Bunyip says, use of anything made by humans, but I don't think the game will break or anything if an ST decides 'honoring' a thing means more than just using it, but considering it worthy in and of itself. One might decide that just entering a human dwelling to get shelter from the rain is fine, but that intentionally acquiring a human abode for long-term residence, being house-proud of it, etc, is more in breach of the ban.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut then, an ST's ability to interpret something is one of the great variables of any game, and will change from table to table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And wearing clothing is utilitarian, while going shopping for style is honoring the clothes (and a very human process). Learning to drive a car is a skill that can help your pack hunt better, by traveling faster than feet will take them (even with gifts). Pimpin' y0 ride is honoring the work of human hands; for that matter so is bitch-slapping the dude who sits on your car, or keyed it. A gun, specifically chosen for a task you know the pack can't do another way (and this is more of a stretch) is just a tool; packing heat as a matter of course because that's how you expect things to go down is honoring man's implements of war. Ditto for edged weaponry.<br /> <br /> If you approach PK's ban from a functional and attitudinal perspective you can even imagine one of them using computers on a daily basis, because they have to for the work that supports the pack and its hunts. Using a computer to surf YouTube vids of Big Bang Theory re-runs would be a breaking point towards flesh.<br /> <br /> Human work is to be exploited only as much as necessary, and discarded immediately thereafter. Think of them as the Sith of Father Wolf's children: they form no attachments to human work, and destroy such things if they grow attached to them. (Now, that fetish you just made is another matter, as is the hand-spun fiber garment your packmate gave you for Wolfmas.)<br /> <br /> In some respects the PK could be <i>easier</i> to represent than the Fire-Touched, because while the PK need to screw their attitudes to the right place with action that follows, the FT need to constantly attend to themselves that they do not knowlingly lie. The tongue is notoriously hard to govern....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS Edit: Obviously there's a wide range of portrayals that could be used, however &quot;feral tribe of the wood&quot; is a trope that only fits part of the time and I think the developers would prefer that each of the Pure be viable in any given setting, with consideration. Otherwise they're pigeon-holed badly, and that seems to be what 2e wants to escape from, broadly speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 05-18-2018, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T08:58:42-07:00","id":1219980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219933#post1219933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would be Breaking Points for Predator Kings Ban? Using Firearms/clothing/house?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219936#post1219936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything made by humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, this make me thinking - So Predator Kings are totally fine if you made things <i>yourself </i>( as werewolf ). So the wooden hut in woods is good - if <i>you build it</i>, by your own hands. RV / Camper can be used - if <b>only werewolves </b>build it, from scratch. So Predator Kings can have <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outlaw_motorcycle_club\" target=\"_blank\">Motorcycle Club packs</a>, in the end! They just need to <i>really</i> made their own workshop with each. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I can see Predator Kings in uniforms - if they sew them themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-18-2018, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:08:21-07:00","id":1219982,"title":"","content":"As to whole quote from <b>WtF</b> 2E core: <i>'The Predator Kings can\u2019t use the fruits of human labor, which puts them on the back foot already, but you can tighten the screws further \u2014 chase or lure them into human buildings, that sort of thing. Make them choose \u2014 break their oath or suffer.'</i><br /> <br /> Make me think about Terminator 1 &amp; 2 movies where humans run down in to factories, to use machines to kill the robots. Now exchange Sarah Connor for Forsaken and Terminators for Pure - and you get a scene where Uratha specially goes into factories, sets the traps with human machinery - and see how Pure need to brake their Ban or die crashed by a hydraulic press. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:12:46-07:00","id":1219983,"title":"","content":"As we have Predators Kings more or less talked about - I want to point onto Ivory Claws Tribal Vow and how they should work with 2E Harmony. IC Vow states:<br /> '<i>Call no whelp of lesser blood your brother or sister</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.'<br /> <br /> So what, their Ban is only shown if someone other call their packmates to come from Forsaken? Only on this Ban can be broken?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:24:11-07:00","id":1219987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219884#post1219884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribal Bans have been...altered. It is a breaking point towards Flesh, yes. And it could come under the Ban condition, inflicting penalties to breaking it and earning beats whilst Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a>, I think you are partially wrong - Violating Oath of<i><b> the Moon</b></i> is Breaking Point toward Flesh, and for Forsaken only.<br /> <br /> <i>Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, \u20132) </i><br /> <br /> I do not see Harmony Breaking Points examples for Pure and their Oath of Urfarah, sadly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <b>Dear forumers, what would be you point on the matter of Breaking Points from Tribal Ban for Pure IF they do not work like for Forsaken?</b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:57:08-07:00","id":1220002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219983#post1219983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what, their Ban is only shown if someone other call their packmates to come from Forsaken? Only on this Ban can be broken?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems about having family members who are Forsaken, which ties into the importance they have for lineage and 'Pure'ity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-18-2018, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T12:03:53-07:00","id":1220047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1220002#post1220002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems about having family members who are Forsaken, which ties into the importance they have for lineage and 'Pure'ity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to depend greatly upon definitions of &quot;lesser blood&quot; and &quot;brother&quot;. At its laxest, a Pure could still have a peaceable relationship with Forsaken, provided they aren't &quot;close&quot; (like a business relationship, or casual association). &quot;Lesser blood&quot; implies that considering humans and non-Uratha (probably Wolf-blooded as well) as family is verboten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T16:03:14-07:00","id":1220125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219980#post1219980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I can see Predator Kings in uniforms - if they sew them themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Usually with the interwoven skulls of their greatest kills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T16:09:12-07:00","id":1220127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219987#post1219987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a>, I think you are partially wrong - Violating Oath of<i><b> the Moon</b></i> is Breaking Point toward Flesh, and for Forsaken only.<br /> <br /> <i>Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, \u20132) </i><br /> <br /> I do not see Harmony Breaking Points examples for Pure and their Oath of Urfarah, sadly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <b>Dear forumers, what would be you point on the matter of Breaking Points from Tribal Ban for Pure IF they do not work like for Forsaken?</b><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same metaphysical principles-your spiritual makeup is bound up in a resonant code, so breaking it is a breaking point towards the Flesh. The Oath of Urfarah is no different from the Oath of the Moon on that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1219980#post1219980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, this make me thinking - So Predator Kings are totally fine if you made things <i>yourself </i>( as werewolf ). So the wooden hut in woods is good - if <i>you build it</i>, by your own hands. RV / Camper can be used - if <b>only werewolves </b>build it, from scratch. So Predator Kings can have <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outlaw_motorcycle_club\" target=\"_blank\">Motorcycle Club packs</a>, in the end! They just need to <i>really</i> made their own workshop with each. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I can see Predator Kings in uniforms - if they sew them themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Step One: Build the oven.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this is probably not an unfair reading, but keep in mind the limits-the Predator Kings may be completely able to exploit this approach, but much of their attitude is rooted in an anti-civilization attitude. Clothes they made, weapons they made, even vehicles they made, sure, but keep in mind that they strip things back more and more. They really think the meaning of life is the early days of wolf and man. These guys are like the Red Talons of Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't have a Predator King Motorcycle Club with werewolves who all made their own bikes from scratch, but I am saying that is really pulling against their mentality, and does not create a precedent for common behavior within the Tribe itself.<br /> <br /> EDIT: THis was going to be two posts, but then I remembered I could just edit this into the previous post, and so I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-18-2018, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T17:54:48-07:00","id":1220142,"title":"","content":"They are as problematic as any other tribal Oath. As with all the others, the Predator King's ban is up to the individual interpretation. Some might think no man made material can touch his hands, others might interpret it as fine so long as they don't exalt the man made product. In the same way what 'Sacred Place' means in the Hunter ban, or 'Honoring' your territory means for the Iron Masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T17:55:15-07:00","id":1220143,"title":"","content":"The Pure book had a Predator King motorcycle gang pack. The Pure are big into sinning and paying penance later, rather than avoiding it to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T20:24:42-07:00","id":1220169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1220143#post1220143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure book had a Predator King motorcycle gang pack. The Pure are big into sinning and paying penance later, rather than avoiding it to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's how they condone virtual genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T03:09:42-07:00","id":1220215,"title":"","content":"One thing I've done in my home brew is to make a mechanic that extends Aspirations to represent common motives within supernatural subgroups in a way that promote play that fits with Canon. In Werewolf this came down to Tribal Ban, Auspice/Pure, and Pack Aspiration. Defining these common desires as Aspirations also have the benefit of giving common understanding of motives, which is applicable in Social Manuevering as any other Aspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801807#post801807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Shared Aspirations</b></span><br /> Each Major Template gain three Aspirations beyond their three Personal Aspirations, for mages these are Arcane Aspirations which is a source of Arcane Beats and thus Arcane Experience, vampires have Requiem Aspirations which is a source of Requiem Beat and thus Requiem Experience, werewolves have Primal Aspirations which are a source of Primal Beats and thus Primal Experience, changelings have Stray Aspirations which are a source of Stray Beats and thus Stray Experience, Sin-Eaters have Ossurary Aspirations which are a source of Ossurary Beats and thus Ossurary Experience. These different aspirations often define the unifying goals of the groups they represent, and/or promote styles of play conducive to maintaining themes and motifs presented in Chronicles of Darkness canon. These Aspirations are by definition implied to already exist in the source material but in Frailty Chronicles we assign mechanical weight to them to reward playing to type and promote play consistent with the canon setting. Also let it be pointed out these are the types of Experiences that are spent on supernatural powers and benefits, which are often the most sought after mechanics to add to characters, so the motivation to play towards canon should be significant. Aspirations that naturally fit character types it promotes play consistent with those character types, and rewards playing towards type, making a more consistent setting. Many role players may want to play a special snowflake, but universal application of that trend is detrimental for a cohesive fiction or internally consistent world<br /> <br /> ...snip...<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Experience</b> is earned from beats gotten from Conditions gain in the Sacred Hunt, and from pursuing Auspice, Tribe and Pack Aspirations<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice/Pure Aspiration (Static)</b><br /> <b>Irraka: </b>Out-smart and out-maneuver the prey<br /> <b>Ithaeur: </b>Seek the deeper mysteries about the prey<br /> <b>Elidoth: </b>Respect the dignity of the prey<br /> <b>Cahalith: </b>Cause the prey to flee by letting it know that it is hunted<br /> <b>Rahu: </b>Kill the prey with swift mercy<br /> <br /> <b>Pure: </b>Punish the Forsaken for the death of Urfidum<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe Aspirations (Static)</b><br /> <b>Iron Masters: </b>Respect your territory in all things<br /> <b>Boneshadow:</b> Repay a spirit for how it has treated you and yours<br /> <b>Stormlord: </b>Conceal your weakness from friend and foe<br /> <b>Blood Talons</b>: Bravely stand against foes<br /> <b>Hunters in the darkness: </b>Defend or avenge a sacred place<br /> <br /> <b>Predator King: </b>Achieve all goals without human tools<br /> <b>Fire Touched: </b>Always challenge falsehood<br /> <b>Ivory Claws:</b> Treat those of lesser lineage as lesser<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Aspiration</b>: This Aspiration is chosen by Pack Consensus, and is gained by the whole pack when earned. This is to promote teamwork and pack mentality.<br /> <br /> ...snip...<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This means Pure trying to persuade or intimidate other Pure into Punishing the Forsaken or following the Tribal Ban gain the benefits in Opening Doors for pushing in a direction and Aspiration already goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also if you think of these as Aspirations, which is a fair way to thinking of them, then they aren't impossibly harsh.Predator King's don't technically need human made things since they can eat as wolves and make anything they need for themselves. Also since it isn't like a Bane which damages them they merely need to Break towards Spirit in standard Werewolf to recover Balance, like Eating Humans, after they deal with the Breaking Point Condition.... Predator King's that happily eat people?? Sounds like a pre-existing stereotype to me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T10:56:21-07:00","id":1220280,"title":"","content":"So, you've basically gentrified stereotypes in your setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T20:47:24-07:00","id":1220705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1220280#post1220280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you've basically gentrified stereotypes in your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've made it so playing to type within Canon has actual rewards, encouraging a setting that at least partially resembles canon. I've seen many a game, particularly in large scale LARPs, where players choose their character's group memberships like they are solely a buffet of powers and not actual in world organizations or groups sharing common motivations. I've noticed groups in real life share goals and motives, since motivation is part of what define one group from another. I think giving mechanical consequences of story elements such as the Social Maneuvering taking into account Aspirations that would reflect the in world group's motivations gives the whole setting more 'life'. Besides, who doesn't like additional opportunity for XP, and isn't it all the better if that XP helps explains trends in behavior?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T06:58:46-07:00","id":1220822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1219870-how-problematic-are-pure-tribes-vows?p=1220705#post1220705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've made it so playing to type within Canon has actual rewards, encouraging a setting that at least partially resembles canon. I've seen many a game, particularly in large scale LARPs, where players choose their character's group memberships like they are solely a buffet of powers and not actual in world organizations or groups sharing common motivations. I've noticed groups in real life share goals and motives, since motivation is part of what define one group from another. I think giving mechanical consequences of story elements such as the Social Maneuvering taking into account Aspirations that would reflect the in world group's motivations gives the whole setting more 'life'. Besides, who doesn't like additional opportunity for XP, and isn't it all the better if that XP helps explains trends in behavior?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that is an issue with the player, not the game. I don't need Totemic-like aspirations from from my Firstborn, if it captured my loyalty, I'd come up with my own personal aspirations in relation to my tribal patron, expressively based on the uniqueness of my own character. For example: If I had an Elodoth Blood Talon who's prone to leave a trail of crippled, tortured Oath-breakers and Pure, who behaves more like a serial killer would and will inconspicuously kidnap them, how would that even begin to resemble &quot;respecting the dignity of my prey&quot; or &quot;stand bravely against my opponent&quot;? But hey, you do you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}